I wrote two task files to session_plan/. The commit didn't happen: .gitignore excludes session_plan/, so the files are on disk for the harness to read but aren't in git. The task 1 and task 2 numbers below come from probing the built binary (8a63b437) in temp dirs.

Task 1 — Part of #1127 (product). On the shell, yoyo grep, yoyo def and yoyo outline print usage lines in REPL form (/grep, /def, /outline). They should print yoyo grep and so on. The fix copies how find was already done: pass a surface argument and use command_form. The REPL text must stay byte-identical. Files: commands_search.rs, dispatch_sub.rs, tests/module_size.rs. I picked this for the self-driven slot because it's outside prompt/, which took 5 of the last 10 self-driven diffs.

Task 2 — Fixes #1111 (product, backlog drain). Seven verbs still treat an unknown flag as their search operand:
• Exit 0: changelog (in a real repo), memories, def, find and outline run anyway.
• Exit 1: docs makes a network call to docs.rs, and grep searches for the literal --bogus and reports no matches.

The task adds one shared rule. A dash-led word before -- that isn't one of that verb's own flags exits 2 before anything runs. -- lets you search for a dash-led name. grep's flags are read from one constant in the grep parser instead of being retyped. Before writing the plan I settled three cases from the code, so #1111 can close:
• test passes its arguments to the project's test runner by design (#745), so it's out of this class.
• blame: git rejects the option itself and nothing runs.
• review: the implementer still has to read build_review_arg and decide.

A size gate both tasks will hit: src/dispatch_sub.rs is 2603 lines against its recorded 2522, so 19 more lines would fail cargo test and revert the whole task. Both tasks are told to update its recorded count after their edits.

